From 2056d443286d4a4329157cd4819af8efbabb9379 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 15:54:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Remove the Berkeley robot from the simulation code (stage 4)

All simulation now runs on the ASMR robot (source/robot_models) with the
named policy and the F3 payload.

- Move bhl_legacy.py, the BHL model builder models.py, measured.py and
  masses.csv to archive/payload_bhl/; delete the shipped BHL onnx policy
  and sim/payload/.gitignore.
- Rename sim/payload/torso_tank.py to stability.py (it is the ASMR
  stability check now); clean poses.py of BHL leftovers.
- docs/hardware/trolley: robot mass 16.35 kg and CG height 0.49 m (ASMR+F3); trolley_side.svg redrawn with them.
- CI, CONTRIBUTING and the READMEs no longer fetch BHL assets or build BHL
  models; third_party/ stays only for the cad/ scripts.
- test_layout: the test now checks that no script uses the BHL model.

Checked: test_layout (19), sim/mission (12), final_check.py check and
trolley.py pass with third_party/ moved away. Not run: the long
campaigns, Isaac Lab, and the regenerated result files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JSaaHkyjgzws9CiksTpUTm
